kubernetes schedular is respnsible for scheduling pods and nodes

schedular is only responsible for deciding which pod goes on which node
it doesnt actually place the pod on node
thats actually done by kubelet(located in the worker node)


schedular is only responsible for deciding which pod goes on which node depending on criteria
how does scheduler assign these pods

schduler looks at each pod and find the best node for it
for ex: a pod needs 10cpu
it looks at each node and calculate no of cpus available, the depoloys the podthe cpu with highest available cpu or with some algo

kube_schedular setup

download kube_schedular from kubernetes release page
extract it and run it as a service
cat /etc/systemd/system/kube-schedular.service

kubeadm tool
it depoloys kube_schedular as a pod 
you can view it in 
cat /etc/kubernetes/manifests/kube-schedular.yaml

to see running process for kube_schedular

ps -aux | grep kube-schedular
